WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:05.850
The longest Star Wars movie so far, The Last
Jedi is densely packed with tons of details

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:09.810
and easter eggs that even some die-hard fans
may have missed on a first viewing.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:13.700
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and today I want to talk about some fascinating

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.890
references and hidden details in Episode 8
that have more significance than you might

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:18.980
have initially realised.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:23.410
And if you're new to my channel, I do regular
easter egg videos, movie breakdowns, theories

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.600
and deleted scenes, plus giveaways.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.300
To enter my current Star Wars giveaway, just
make sure you're subscribed and leave me a

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:33.329
comment about any easter eggs or interesting
details you spotted in the film.

00:00:33.329 --> 00:00:37.859
Spoiler warning, I'll be discussing scenes
from The Last Jedi in depth so take care if

00:00:37.859 --> 00:00:39.909
you haven't seen the movie yet.

00:00:39.909 --> 00:00:44.909
After Yoda returned as a Force Ghost, reuniting
with Luke on Acht'To, the legendary Jedi Master

00:00:44.909 --> 00:00:47.519
burned down the island's ancient Force Tree.

00:00:47.519 --> 00:00:51.649
And when Luke protested about the destruction
of the sacred Jedi texts and Yoda replied

00:00:51.649 --> 00:00:55.839
that there was nothing in there "that the
girl Rey does not already possess", it seemed

00:00:55.839 --> 00:00:59.659
that the ancient books had burned with the
Tree, but that Rey had already mastered everything

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.659
in them.

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:04.890
However, Yoda's words actually had another
meaning which became clear at the end of the

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:05.890
movie.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:09.580
There's a crucial moment on the Millennium
Falcon when Finn opens a drawer to get a blanket

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:14.280
to cover the injured Rose Tico, and as Finn
rummages around, you can spot the Jedi books

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:18.220
right there, meaning that Rey actually took
them from the island.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:22.390
So, Yoda's reply to Luke was a clever bit
of wordplay and suggests that Rey has more

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:23.390
to learn.

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:27.280
Of course, it also means that Rey and the
Resistance still have the old Jedi scripts

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:31.630
which they can use to inspire and teach new
Force Users about the Jedi way.

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:36.390
Near the start of the film, Rey tells Luke
that the Resistance needs his help to face

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:38.960
their enemies, and he replies, "You think,
what?

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:42.770
I'm gonna walk out with a laser sword and
face down the whole First Order?"

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:46.840
Luke's use of the word "laser sword" is an
easter egg to George Lucas's early Star Wars

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:51.210
scripts where that term was used instead of
lightsaber; and in The Phantom Menace, we

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.710
hear the same term used by a young Anakin
Skywalker.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:59.370
As well as containing a hat tip to the saga's
origins, Luke's reply to Rey also foreshadows

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:00.700
the end of the movie.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:04.990
In contrast to what he said, Luke does indeed
walk out armed with just a lightsaber and

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:07.310
confront the entire First Order.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:11.770
And yet, Luke also stays true to his original
words to Rey, because it's not actually his

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:15.989
physical self who faces down the First Order,
but rather a Force Projection.

00:02:15.989 --> 00:02:22.090
Ahch-To is home to the first Jedi temple which
has a curious ancient mosaic on its floor

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:25.890
of the Prime Jedi, the very first member of
the Jedi Order.

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:30.810
The mosaic's design is reminiscent of a yin-yang
symbol and shows the Prime Jedi "in a state

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:35.099
of meditation and balance", which foreshadows
Luke's own position on the island at the end

00:02:35.099 --> 00:02:36.159
of the movie.

00:02:36.159 --> 00:02:40.210
The image also shows a fusion of light and
dark, which is interesting because in The

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:45.840
Last Jedi, Rey and Kylo Ren form a force bond
between them and Kylo asks Rey to join him.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:50.420
Of course, the mosaic also symbolises the
tension that Force Users experience of being

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:53.190
pulled between the light and the dark sides.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:57.599
For example, Kylo struggles with his connection
to the dark side and experiences a "pull to

00:02:57.599 --> 00:02:59.120
the light", as he calls it.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:04.329
There's a clear parallel between the hole
that Rey climbs into on the Jedi Temple island

00:03:04.329 --> 00:03:08.439
and the Dark Side cave that Luke entered during
his training on Dagobah.

00:03:08.439 --> 00:03:11.329
Both the caves force the entrant to confront
their worst fear.

00:03:11.329 --> 00:03:15.810
For Luke, this appeared to be the evil that
Darth Vader represented, but when the cave

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:19.970
exposed Luke's face inside Vader's helmet,
it showed that Luke's real fear was that he

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:24.989
might turn to the Dark side, and it also foreshadowed
the reveal that he was Darth Vader's son.

00:03:24.989 --> 00:03:29.450
Although we don't hear the reveal of Rey's
parents until later in The Last Jedi, we do

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:33.519
get an interesting bit of foreshadowing via
Rey's experience in the cave.

00:03:33.519 --> 00:03:37.790
Rey's always been waiting for her parents
to return to her, but when she sees her own

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:41.849
image endlessly reflected back to her, it
foreshadows the discovery later that she's

00:03:41.849 --> 00:03:46.319
actually known the answer within herself all
along, in other words she is alone.

00:03:46.319 --> 00:03:50.719
Or as Maz Kanata said in The Force Awakens,
'whomever you're waiting for [...], they're

00:03:50.719 --> 00:03:51.719
never coming back.'

00:03:51.719 --> 00:03:57.629
In a call-back to the time Luke crash-landed
in a swamp on Dagobah in The Empire Strikes

00:03:57.629 --> 00:04:01.340
Back, there's a submerged X-wing on the shores
of the Jedi Temple island.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:05.830
And Luke has salvaged an S-foil from that
underwater X-wing to make a door for his stone

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:07.920
hut on Ahch'To.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:12.790
In The Last Jedi, we get to meet Snoke close
up and although we still don't know his backstory,

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:17.510
there's one item he owns which reveals some
secrets about his connection to the Dark Side.

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:21.350
The gold ring the Supreme Leader wears on
his finger is etched with symbols of the Four

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:23.100
Sages of Dwartii.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:27.530
The Four Sages were philosophers from the
planet Dwartii who, in the early days of the

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:31.100
Republic, stirred controversy, promoted the
study of the Dark Side of the Force, and were

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.890
popular among the Sith.

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:37.410
In fact, Palpatine had statues of them in
his office in Attack of the Clones.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:41.600
Snoke also has a link to another legendary
Sith Lord, as the black stone in the ring

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:46.290
is actually obsidian mined from the catacombs
below Darth Vader's Castle on the volcanic

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:51.320
planet Mustafar, which was also the location
of Anakin and Obi-Wan's fateful duel in Revenge

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:53.030
of the Sith.

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:57.220
The way Poe Dameron toys with General Hux
at the start of the film, pretending he can't

00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:01.340
hear him and is waiting to be patched through
by Hux's communications officer, is reminiscent

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:06.040
of the start of The Force Awakens where Poe
made fun of Kylo Ren after being captured,

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:10.760
asking who should talk first and saying it
was hard to understand him through the mask.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:15.290
And in The Last Jedi, Poe's line, "Tell [Hux]
Leia has an urgent message for him... about

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:19.340
his mother" is a dig at the fact that Hux
is an illegitimate child whose mother was

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:24.070
a kitchen worker, a fact which was revealed
in a recent canon Star Wars novel.

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:29.680
Speaking of Poe, after he struck up a bromance
with ex-stormtrooper Finn in The Force Awakens,

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:33.850
it was nice to see them reunite when Finn
woke up in his Bacta suit.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:37.590
And after Finn got dressed, he donned Poe's
old jacket which, if you look carefully, you

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:42.360
can see has been repaired after Finn's run-in
with Kylo Ren in Episode 7.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:46.961
In fact, it was Poe who stitched the jacket
back up while Finn was recovering, a detail

00:05:46.961 --> 00:05:50.390
I'm sure fans of Stormpilot will particularly
like.

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:55.860
BB-8 got to do some pretty cool things in
The Last Jedi and, while on board the Supremacy,

00:05:55.860 --> 00:06:00.430
Finn disguised him with a black metal can
making him resemble a rather large mouse droid.

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:04.940
He even scoots along making noises that are
uncannily similar and match the pattern made

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:07.930
by an MSE-6 repair droid in A New Hope.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:13.170
To top it all, BB-8 also bumps into a Stormtrooper
on the Supremacy, just like the mouse droid

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:18.060
ran into Han and Luke disguised as Stormtroopers
alongside Chewie in Episode 4.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:22.710
After Leia recovers from her time in space,
there's a nice call back to one of her first

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:24.210
scenes in A New Hope.

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:28.280
When she bursts through the door to confront
the mutinous Poe Dameron, she's dressed in

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:33.830
white like we saw her in Episode 4 and she
uses her blaster in stun mode on Poe, sending

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:38.560
out blue circular blasts, just how the Stormtroopers
blasted Leia to catch her at the beginning

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:40.460
of A New Hope.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:44.680
Leia's scenes in The Last Jedi have, of course,
taken on an added poignancy since Carrie Fisher

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:45.890
passed away.

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:50.420
And although it's unclear what exactly will
happen with Leia in Episode 9, Episode 8 was

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:55.250
a real Fisher family affair, with both her
daughter Billie Lourd playing Lieutenant Connix

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:58.890
again, and the additional bonus of a space
cameo by Carrie's dog Gary.

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:04.100
Look out for him on Canto Bight in the casino
scene where an alien dog appears whose design

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:08.000
was based on the much-loved actress's famous
pet.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:11.560
During the battle on Crait, the Millennium
Falcon loses its radar dish again.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:16.220
As Chewie tries to outmanoeuvre some TIE fighters,
the ship gets caught in a tight spot in some

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:21.360
underground caves and one of the TIE fighters
gets a shot on the sensor dish, blasting it

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:22.360
off.

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:25.900
The original circular sensor dish was lost
when Lando flew the Falcon in Return of the

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:27.750
Jedi.

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:32.430
The astonishing ending to The Last Jedi also
has some important easter eggs and call-backs

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:37.030
from binary sunsets on Tatooine, to Sith force
projections, and Luke becoming one with the

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:38.030
Force.

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:42.310
I go into detail on these and more in my Last
Jedi ending explained video as well as talking

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:43.800
theories on Episode 9.

